{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-256191-r4525570","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Tuna Melt Fishcakes","sourcePageId":256191,"sourceRevision":"4525570","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-21T02:33:08Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tuna%20Melt%20Fishcakes&oldid=4525570","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:27.026Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:Low-GI recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using basil","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using caper","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using lemon","Category:Recipes using parmesan","Category:Recipes using ricotta","Category:Recipes using tuna","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"d4d97f5d12b9f4200b80ce6306ab58017d653016a43039bc7ddd3aa06ade42fb","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Fish recipes|servings=4|time=45 minutes|difficulty=1}}{{recipe}}\n\nThis practical and tasty recipe can be served either hot or cold as a fast main course or for a picnic or a buffet.\n\n== Ingredients == \n* 200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Tuna|tuna]] in [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n* 200 g [[Cookbook:Ricotta|ricotta cheese]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Eggs|eggs]]\n* 50 g [[Cookbook:Caper|capers]]\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Breadcrumbs|breadcrumbs]]\n* 50 g grated [[Cookbook:Parmigiano Reggiano|parmesan cheese]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]] or [[Cookbook:Basil|basil]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]], zested and juiced\n* [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|Olive oil]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 180ºC before beginning preparation.\n# In a bowl beat the eggs and mix in well the drained tuna with the ricotta.\n# Add a little salt and pepper, the lemon zest, basil or parsley, Parmesan and half the bread crumbs.\n# Distribute a trickle of olive oil in an [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|ovenproof dish]].\n# Work the ingredients well and, with the help of two spoons, form medium-sized balls to be covered in the other half of the breadcrumbs and lay them in the ovenproof dish.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] in the [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] for 25–30 minutes and serve warm or cold drizzling with lemon juice and accompanied by a green salad.\n\n\n[[Category:Recipes using tuna]]\n[[Category:Recipes using caper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ricotta]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]] \n[[Category:Low-GI recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using basil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parmesan]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon]]\n\n[[it:Libro di cucina/Ricette/Polpette di tonno e ricotta]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Tuna Melt Fishcakes","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"200 g tuna in olive oil","sourceText":"200 g tuna in olive oil","amountText":"200 g tuna in olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"200 g ri