sley, Parmesan and half the bread crumbs.","sourceText":"Add a little salt and pepper, the lemon zest, basil or parsley, Parmesan and half the bread crumbs.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Distribute a trickle of olive oil in an ovenproof dish.","sourceText":"Distribute a trickle of olive oil in an ovenproof dish.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Work the ingredients well and, with the help of two spoons, form medium-sized balls to be covered in the other half of the breadcrumbs and lay them in the ovenproof dish.","sourceText":"Work the ingredients well and, with the help of two spoons, form medium-sized balls to be covered in the other half of the breadcrumbs and lay them in the ovenproof dish.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Bake in the oven for 25–30 minutes and serve warm or cold drizzling with lemon juice and accompanied by a green salad.","sourceText":"Bake in the oven for 25–30 minutes and serve warm or cold drizzling with lemon juice and accompanied by a green salad.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:256191","recordId":"wikibooks-256191-r4525570","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4525570","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tuna%20Melt%20Fishcakes&oldid=4525570","sourceSha256":"d4d97f5d12b9f4200b80ce6306ab58017d653016a43039bc7ddd3aa06ade42fb","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless oth